# review-of-stage-high: not delivered, and only ONE statement is left in front of it

**NO-GO on the obligation.** `agents/tasks/LJ-1-565/Probe565.agda::stage-high`
is not inhabited and no postulate stands in for it. `StageHigh` is
`[LJ-1.536]`'s type, imported and not restated
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/Probe536.agda:350-352`, imported at
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-565/Probe565.agda:45`). The probe is green: exit 0,
`runs/full-t2.out`, median **26.92 s** and 612 MB over three cold runs
(`runs/full-t1.time`, `runs/full-t2.time`, `runs/full-t3.time`).

**BUT THIS IS NOT THE SAME NO-GO AS THE LAST TWO.** `Probe565.agda:327-328`:

    stage-high-from-limit : HierBelowLimitH → StageHigh
    stage-high-from-limit lim = reduction (allH→all (closing lim))

**`StageHigh` NOW RESTS ON EXACTLY ONE OPEN STATEMENT**, and that statement is
the limit case. Everything else between it and the trophy is a green term.

## The brief's question, answered

**THE DOOR IS PAID AND THE DOOR WAS NEVER THE BLOCKER.** `AtStage` applies at
`[LJ-1.536]`'s formula with both hypotheses fed: `runs/W3.agda:78-81`, green on
its first run, median 2.15 s (`runs/w3-t1.time`, `runs/w3-t2.time`,
`runs/w3-t3.time`). So `[LJ-1.562]`'s finding reaches this site.

**AND IT CHANGES NOTHING HERE, BECAUSE `[LJ-1.536]` NEVER STOOD AT THAT DOOR.**
That task built its formula straight at `⟪ Lset σ ⟫` and went through
`𝒟ₒ-intro` (`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/Probe536.agda:212-213`, `:293-295`), green.
`carve∈𝒟ₒ` (`src/L/Axioms/Separation.lagda.md:198-199`) takes a formula at
`⟪ Lset σ ⟫ ` and nothing else: no `Δ₀`, no `BoundedFo`, no restriction on its
quantifiers. The two hypotheses buy the satisfaction bridge from an EXTERNAL
formula (`:163-168`); they do not buy the way in. `Probe565.agda:93-94` is that
as a term.

**THE STOP NAMED A SECOND REASON AND THE BRIEF ASKED ME TO SAY SO. IT DID.**
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/review-of-StageHigh.md:88-91`, "THE LIMIT DID NOT
LEAVE", and its report names a third at
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md:220-231`, the successor row that
exhausts 8 GB.

## What actually blocked it

**THE THIRD REASON WAS THE NEAR WALL, AND ITS PUBLISHED DIAGNOSIS IS WRONG.**
`[LJ-1.536]` attributes that row's cost to two spellings of a finite successor
tower and concludes "98 PERCENT OF THE COST IS `sucV`"
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md:248`). `runs/Control565c.agda` makes
NO stage move at all, spells the stage the same way on both sides, and still
exhausts 11.05 GB (`runs/ctlc-0.time`). `runs/Control565f.agda` repeats it with
the second name written out locally: 10.94 GB (`runs/ctlf-0.time`).

**THE CAUSE IS THE `isL` WITNESS, AND IT IS A CONTROLLED PAIR.**

| file | the witness | result |
|---|---|---|
| `runs/Control565c.agda:40-43` | computed by `isL-ord` at `sucV α` | **HEAP WALL, 11.05 GB, 263.63 s** |
| `runs/Control565g.agda:49-53` | a PARAMETER, nothing else changed | **exit 0, 1.93 s** |

`HierBelow` computes it (`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/Probe536.agda:186-187` through
`:135-136`), and `isL-ord` bottoms out in `ord∈Lset-suc`, which is
`∈-induction` (`src/L/Ordinal/Stages.lagda.md:434-435`) applied to a
TRANSPARENT `sucV α`. Two further controls bracket it: forming the type is free
at 1.93 s (`runs/Control565d.agda`, `runs/ctld-0.time`) and comparing
`hierL (sucV α) h o` with itself at an abstract witness is free at 1.44 s
(`runs/Control565e.agda`, `runs/ctle-0.time`).

**I DID NOT READ THE MECHANISM OUT OF AGDA AND I DO NOT ASSERT IT.** What is
measured is the differential.

## What that bought

**THE NEAR WALL IS BROKEN.** Attempt 1 of this task built four routes to the
successor step and every one walled
(`runs/attempt-1-review-of-stage-high.md.preserved`). Every one targeted
`HierBelow (sucV α) (suc-ord oα)`. Targeting the witness-abstract statement
instead:

| row | where | price |
|---|---|---|
| the successor step | `Probe565.agda:212-219` | exit 0, **27.37 s** (`runs/ctlh-0.time`) |
| the bridge back, at a VARIABLE γ | `:232-234` | exit 0, **1.95 s** (`runs/ctlw-0.time`) |
| the whole induction | `:289-309` | exit 0, **24.34 s** (`runs/ctlx-0.time`) |

**AND THE TRANSPORT THAT WALLED TWICE FOR ATTEMPT 1 IS GONE, NOT CURED.** Its
`MoveAlong` carries the obligation along `sucV δ ≡ γ` and walled at 8 GB in two
independent forms (`runs/ctls-0.out`, `runs/ctlt-0.out`). Here the motive
quantifies over both witnesses (`Probe565.agda:236-237`), so the move is a
plain `subst` and no `PathP` and no uniqueness law appears at that step.

**THE ORDINAL SPLIT IS ATTEMPT 1'S AND THE CREDIT IS ITS OWN.**
`runs/Control565v.agda`, free at 1.84 s (`runs/ctlv-0.out`), restated at
`Probe565.agda:259-268` because a control is not a module to import from.

## What is left, and why I stopped

**`HierBelowLimitH` (`Probe565.agda:285-287`), AND NOTHING ELSE.** At a limit γ
the members of `hierL γ` are the pairs `pr c (Lset c)` for c ∈ γ; to carve that
set out of a stage the formula must say "w is the tower's value at c" inside the
stage, which is the level formula, `Σ₁`, with the existential over an
approximation unbounded at the ambient level
(`dev/literature/devlin-II5.md:217`).

**THE BRIEF ORDERS THE STOP HERE** and I take it: "IF THE REAL BLOCKER IS AN
UNBOUNDED SEARCH, SAY SO AND STOP. `[LJ-1.560]` is running on exactly that
question and this brief must not duplicate it."

**AND I DO NOT OVERSTATE IT.** Attempt 1 wrote that it "did not reach the limit
case and it measured nothing about it". **NEITHER DID THIS ATTEMPT.** That the
limit case IS `[LJ-1.560]`'s question is an argument from
`dev/literature/devlin-II5.md:217` and `:221-222` together with
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md`'s `## FOR THE NEXT BRIEF` point 2. It
is not a measurement, and `stage-high-from-limit` does not depend on it. **So
this is a second site by argument and not by measurement, and the brief's
"CONFIRM from a second site" is only half earned.**

## One thing the reader must know before trusting any citation here

**I DESTROYED PART OF ATTEMPT 1'S RECORD.** I overwrote its `Probe565.agda`,
its `runs/W3.agda` and its `runs/Control565a.agda` through `Control565h.agda`
before reading them, so its report's citations to those paths now resolve to my
files. The full accounting is in `lj-1.565-report.md`, `## THE RECORD I
DAMAGED`. Its report and its stop survive verbatim at
`runs/attempt-1-report.md.preserved` and
`runs/attempt-1-review-of-stage-high.md.preserved`.
